## Day 4: Product Performance Analysis
📊 Business Problem

The sales team wants to understand which products are driving sales and which products are underperforming. Management needs a simple dashboard to compare product performance and identify the best-selling products.

##🗂️ Dataset

AdventureWorks-style sales dataset with 3 source tables:

-cust_info — customer demographics
-prd_info — product catalog (product line, cost, pricing history)
-sales_details — transactional sales data (orders, quantity, price)

##🎯 KPIs Tracked

-Total Sales
-Total Quantity Sold
-Total Orders
-Total Products

## 📈 Visuals
-Bar chart: Sales by Product
-Bar chart: Quantity Sold by Product
-Donut chart: Sales by Product Line
-Line chart: Sales by Month
-Table: Top 10 Products by Sales
-Slicers: Product Line, Product, Date

##🛠️ Tools Used

-Power BI Desktop, Power Query, DAX

##💡 Key Learnings

-Practiced analyzing sales at the product level
-Learned to use bar and column charts for comparisons
-Practiced sorting and filtering products by sales
-Learned how slicers affect multiple visuals
-Practiced creating a Top N view
-Improved understanding of relationships between product and sales tables

